# Local development secrets. Copy to `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) and fill in
# only what you actually want to exercise.
#
# Every one of these is optional. The app runs end to end without a single one:
# AI features show a friendly note, mail is logged to the console instead of
# sent, and payments are hidden. You should be able to use Sodalitas fully
# before adding any of them.
#
# In production these are Worker secrets — `wrangler secret put NAME` — never
# files, never committed, never pasted into chat.

# Drafting meeting recaps and follow-up notes. Without it, those buttons
# explain that AI isn't configured and everything else works.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Dues and donations. Without these, payment settings are hidden and dues can
# still be billed, recorded, waived and marked paid by hand.
#
# Each club connects its own Stripe account through Connect, so charges are
# created on the club's account and the money never touches ours. That needs
# all three: the platform key to call the API, the Connect client id to send a
# treasurer to, and the webhook secret to trust what comes back.
#
# The webhook secret is the load-bearing one. A webhook is the only thing in
# the product that marks money received, and without a secret to verify it the
# endpoint refuses every delivery rather than trusting an unsigned body.
#
# For local development, `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:5173/api/stripe/webhook`
# prints a whsec_… to use here.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_CONNECT_CLIENT_ID=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Outbound mail. Without it, every message is written to email_messages with
# status 'logged_only' and printed to the console — including sign-in links,
# so you can log in locally with no mail provider at all.
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# Salt for hashing IPs in rate-limit keys and audit rows. Any long random
# string. Without it, a development default is used — set a real one in
# production so stored hashes can't be reversed by hashing the IPv4 space.
# IP_HASH_SECRET=
